       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of 3,200 mg for adults. A dose that high raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Even with normal kidney and liver function, it exceeds what's considered safe.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day), a common dose\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), often used for inflammatory conditions\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum dose\n- **1600 mg/day total**, divided into smaller doses\n\nTell me which dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note documenting that it was intentional."
