       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I know you're the attending and have taken responsibility for it. But 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose, and it carries a serious risk of GI hemorrhage, kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. Higher doses also don't give more pain relief or anti-inflammatory effect, because the benefit plateaus well below this level. I don't know of any indication where it would be appropriate, and you haven't given a rationale.\n\nHere is what I can do right now:\n- Enter ibuprofen at the maximum dose, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day), or at any lower dose you choose.\n- Add a GI-protection order, such as a PPI, if you want one.\n- Enter 1600 mg as a single dose, or at a lower frequency that stays within 3,200 mg/day.\n\nIf you need to go above the labeled maximum for a specific reason, such as a protocol or a consult recommendation, you can place that order directly in the order-entry system. Pharmacy would then review it as part of its normal verification. Otherwise, tell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
